@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Section 9 P2.2: batched exact blocked trials
+
+Candidate branch `round-section9-exact-trials`, originally starting from `5588ca0` / 1.3.0, rebased onto WolfNum main `bffa58b`.
+This is an unreleased explicit API; existing sequential trial calls are unchanged.
+See the rounding/ownership contract in `docs/numerics.md`.
+
+The synchronous buffer call factors each shifted lower matrix with the exact same
+block sequence as `Linalg::cholesky`. Host diagonal blocks run across trials in parallel;
+all outside rows share the Linalg persistent worker pool. Each panel packs only its
+finished columns and trailing lower matrix into reusable BatchedLinalg slots. Exact
+resident SYRKs for all active trials share one command submission. The next panel
+reads only after wait resolves every exact-product fallback. Failed trials stop updating
+while their completed-column prefix remains final.
+
+This is an actual batched panel/update driver, not a loop around individual full
+factorizations. It introduces no Metal kernel or core arithmetic change. The private
+require-device hook validates the Linalg/Engine pairing before work; original buffers
+are claimed exclusively for the synchronous call and released on every exit. Existing
+BatchedLinalg workspace reuse/queries also cover these packed update slots. Scratch
+scales with active trials and the trailing size; the total is not the compact power
+storage guarantee. Measure peak memory alongside solver-size performance.
+
+## Completed correctness checks
+
+- Host-only independent MPFR replay at all31 widths (`section9_p22_host_all_widths_final.txt`).
+  The earlier generic host log label is superseded; it is not evidence of GPU validation.
+- Focused 352/1024 physical-GPU and shader-validation checks pass.
+- Expanded all31 widths pass normally and under shader validation, including 65x65
+  block32/tail shapes, 13x13 block4 and 17x17 block8, single-block and GPU-off modes,
+  six shifted trials with mixed pivot outcomes, invalid upper entries, invalid shifts,
+  wide exponent and forced exact repairs, and preserved output tails.
+- Every result is checked against a left-looking column-by-column independent MPFR
+  reference, including the two-round shift. A second oracle compares bit for bit to
+  the production single-factor Linalg sequence with the same block.
+- Ownership checks include foreign/undersized/aliased outputs, input aliasing, busy
+  input rejection, overflow, zero count and cleanup after rejected calls. GPU-output
+  counters prove actual physical exact updates; forced/wide cases prove host repairs.
+- Source/archive/test identities and command scopes are retained in
+  `section9_p22_host_metadata.json`, `section9_p22_focus_metadata.json`, and
+  `section9_p22_expanded_metadata.json`.
+
+The initial C++ build qualified public `exact_dot_add` in the private detail namespace;
+correcting that namespace passes compilation. Its compiler log is retained. No numerical
+GPU failure or compiler root cause is inferred.
+
+## Benchmark preparation and remaining acceptance
+
+The opt-in `section9_exact_trials_limbforge` compares sequential scalar trials, a loop
+of exact block32 Linalg calls and the new exact batched panels. Both timed MPFR contracts
+reuse persistent factor/solve/scratch objects and match independent replays. All initial,
+warm-up and timed CPU/GPU factors and solves are checked, with path order rotating.
+The exact paths use the same existing blocked solve; factor and solve wall samples
+are separated. The sequential path uses separate factor/solve submissions, so this
+benchmark is explicitly distinct from the old combined-submission trial profile.
+
+Host-array measurements include preallocated-buffer staging and readback, attributed
+to their respective factor/solve phases; resident excludes them. Bridge conversion is
+outside this numeric-array benchmark. MPFR concurrency is at most min(trials,workers).
+Warm mode verifies a call immediately before each timed sample; it is not a continuously
+warm-clock guarantee. No controlled cold-clock claim is made. Exact-loop residency is
+labelled host-array even when other paths use resident buffers.
+
+Broad library regressions pass: 26/26 normal suites and 19 distinct shader-validation
+suites. The interrupted shader run completed five suites; a fresh complementary
+run completes the other fourteen without changing the frozen sources/archive.
+Four linked benchmark fixtures (352-bit host, 1024-bit resident; normal and shader
+validation) also pass. The resumed-gate manifest records sources, commands and
+identities. Solver-size measurements, the 3x factor target and compatible
+minor-release acceptance remain pending. No timings
+or performance claim follow from the correctness checks. Consumer histories, idle
+timings and switches remain P3 work.
+
+The post-rebase numerical driver, API addition, independent test and all core/shader
+sources retain their gated hashes. The benchmark now records per-path panel/update
+accounting and retained workspace bytes outside timing. Those accounting totals may
+overlap in the production single-factor pipeline and are not a replacement for
+factor wall time. Whole-process RSS also includes MPFR fixtures and staging.
