index 1d5bd85..525eaa3 100644
--- a/docs/numerics.md
+++ b/docs/numerics.md
@@ -1525,3 +1525,31 @@ and both E and outputs are `[steps][4][groups]`. Horner and source scaling have
 contract above. Zero steps/groups writes nothing. With zero terms, E is still multiplied
 by canonical zero, preserving statuses. Outputs contain sources in ascending step order;
 the consumer chooses their application order.
+
+### Candidate exact blocked damping trials (P2.2)
+
+`BatchedLinalg::cholesky_trials_blocked(la, shape, A, D, mu, L, status, options)`
+factors each shifted matrix with precisely the `Linalg::cholesky` block sequence.
+The shift is `RN(A[i,i] + RN(mu[t]*D[i]))`, with two explicit roundings. Inputs are
+shared A `[n][n]`, D `[n]` and mu `[count]`; output is L `[count][n][n]` and uint32
+status `[count]`. Only A's lower triangle is read. Upper output entries are zero.
+Status is zero on success or first failed pivot +1, and failed trials preserve final
+completed columns and invalidate remaining lower columns exactly as Linalg does.
+
+This call is synchronous outside a CommandBatch: independent host panels use the
+Linalg's persistent pool; each panel's exact trailing SYRKs share one submission.
+Every exact-product repair finishes at wait before any subsequent panel reads output.
+`block` determines rounding; GPU placement, host worker count and shared submission
+scheduling do not. `host_macs` applies to the total active trials' trailing work;
+`solve_host_macs` has no effect on factorization. Existing all-device sequential
+trial calls and defaults are unchanged.
+
+Buffers must be idle and belong to this BatchedLinalg's Engine; Linalg must use the
+same Metal device. L/status cannot alias an input or each other. Inputs may alias
+each other. Mapping/submitting original operands while the call runs is rejected.
+On an exception outputs may be partial, and all claimed buffers are released.
+Workspace reuse/release is visible through the existing BatchedLinalg queries.
+Counters report shared panels/submissions, encoded GPU SYRKs, host triangle updates
+and exact-product GPU/fallback output counts; they are not per-trial timings.
+Zero count does no work; positive count requires n>0. This is an unreleased candidate
+with all31 independent references passing normally and under shader validation; broad regressions, measurements and release acceptance remain pending.
